[Music]  Chicharito vegetarian Torito  [Applause]  [Applause]  I actually had a very different video  planned for this week but at the same  time I also wanted to uphold a promise  that I made a while back in my video  about dungeon traversal I asked you guys  to submit some of your ideas regarding  which items you want to see returned or  newly introduced in breadth - Wow -  since I recently hit the glorious 1,000  subscriber milestone I wanted to do  something in return so in this video  I'll be going over some of the ideas  that you submitted now this isn't a top  ten or anything like that the order  doesn't dictate which ideas I like the  most if your idea didn't make it in  don't stress it I will do more viewer  suggestions in the future being able to  communicate with you all and listening  to your feedback and suggestions is  something I enjoy greatly it's what  YouTube is about for me it's not just  visual entertainment it's also a  community at the end of the video I will  also give an update about the channel  and what to expect for me in the near  future but enough of my rambling let's  get started the first suggestion is from  Bret black now when I first read this I  thought wait word a crab claw that's  kind of silly but the more I kept  thinking about it the more amazing the  idea started to become if we are to  assume that Link's green hand will be  able to morph into all kinds of  different shapes and grant him different  abilities a giant claw is actually quite  feasible of course it doesn't have to be  specifically a crab claw could just be a  big hand or Talent  it kind of reminds me of Midna x' hand  from Twilight Princess which she also  uses to grab or deflect giant objects  and is even strong enough to flip beast  Ganon on his side now the Chaika slate  was an amazing item in breath the wild  probably the best item ever to be  introduced when it comes to versatility  however the mag nieces rune although  very cool I thought was fine for puzzle  solving but in terms of combat  implications it was a bit on the slow  side imagine being able to pick up  boulders or other giant objects and  being able to hurl them towards your  enemies or during a boss fight like the  one we saw with master Koga having to  catch giant spike balls launched in your  direction from the air and throwing them  back and as Brett states this would also  double as a progression item essentially  replacing the power brace  LED Titans mid or silver and golden  gauntlets this one's from Seth Falconer  now you suggested a lot of different  ideas but I had to go with the Hylian  guitarman not just because it's awesome  but if we look at some of the early  concept art from brough dewild we can  see that this was in fact something the  zelda team was considering not only that  but we can also see that a motorcycle  was also something that didn't make it  into the base game but eventually did  make it into the DLC since the sequel to  breath the wild was initially supposed  to be DLC 3 the guitar might just have a  chance not a harp or a flute or any of  these weak-ass instruments get out of  here it's about high time link actually  started shredding  [Music]  [Music]  actually this wouldn't even be a first  for link as in majora's mask he also  plays guitar or fishbone wait how does  that even work  this suggestion ties in with two other  comments I got from Peter ganderton and  Gabriel the obsessive who both expressed  a similar desire for the return of  instruments and I agree instruments have  always been something that sets the  series apart and also influences the  music score greatly now I know what  you're thinking if this will indeed be  an electric guitar like the one we see  in the concept art how will it produce  sound without an amplifier one word  magic this was a popular one requested  by knox nintendo 7 and hidden color by  the way sorry if i butcher and of your  names  I think the whip would definitely work  well with breath the wilds engine it's a  tool that is quite versatile since it  can be used for both means of traversal  a way to pull levers from afar and  functions as a weapon or if the wall  didn't make use of any mechanics that  involve having to swing around like we  saw in the Wind Waker Twilight Princess  and Skyward Sword link now has a type of  mobility never before seen in the series  yet there were no additional items to  boost his mobility even further the  closest we came to an upgrade in terms  of mobility was Ravalli scale which was  slow in terms of startup and had limited  use I also want to give an honorable  mention to drew it writer who suggested  the return of the grappling hook from  the Wind Waker which functions very  similar however the whip has a slight  edge over the grappling hook in my  opinion it's faster to use both in terms  of traversal and combat the only thing  the grappling hook has over the whip is  the ability to climb up but if you ask  me that only gives it more reason to  coexist with the modern take on the hook  shot or claw shot which also grants the  player the option to reel themselves in  in the Wind Waker the grappling hook and  hook shot didn't get in each other's way  because one they were introduced very  far apart one in the very first dungeon  and the other in the last one  not counting Ganon's Tower and two both  had clear limitations that made sure  that one would not nullify the other I  think there's a reason why there was no  grappling hook in Twilight Princess  since the clash  had much more options this time around  thus for Skyward Sword which also had to  double claw shot they chose to implement  the whip instead of the grappling hook  being able to disarm enemies from a  distance grab onto designated targets  and swing across gaps or even run along  walls sounds like an absolute blast and  at the same time it wouldn't get in the  way of the hook shot as both have their  limitations next we have sword dashing  suggested by fire hawk all I can say  about this one is yes please we've seen  sword dashing plenty of times in the 2d  games but was never used for the 3d  installments in general it was a bit of  a shame that in breath the wild being  able to run faster was limited to only  nighttime and with specific outfits  equipped sword dashing could work very  well with breath the wilds huge open  world and yet again both for traversing  the landscape as well as using it for  combat introducing the Pegasus boots or  something similar would be a welcome  inclusion and just like in the 2d games  it could even be combined with Lynx  jumping ability and paraglider to scale  greater distances horizontally that's  all I have to say about that one this  one was submitted by Elijah's - and I  gotta say man I'm digging this idea now  I wouldn't say controlling a statue is  very exciting in the past they were  quite slow and clunky to use in combat I  think this idea could be fleshed out  further of course being able to  temporarily possess a non organic object  and have it fight for you is very  appealing and you know what there is  actually something that we could use for  this purpose Hyrule is absolutely  littered with the cave Guardians imagine  being able to take control of one after  all the fear and frustration they put us  through in the first game it would be  nice to have one on our side this time  around depending on if they still have  enough of their legs intact they could  even be able to move we've seen that  even though they are autonomous they are  not immune to being corrupted or taken  over it is time to turn the tide on  Ganondorf and give him a taste of his  own medicine  sir nicholas &amp; Lomb oliver j showed an  interest in a return of the beetle and  well good news this was also found in  the concept art so this one also  definitely has a chance to make it in  especially if Nintendo is planning to  implement unused ideas which in all  probability they will I can definitely  see why people want the beetle to return  as it's a very unique item and one of  the more recent brand-new Zelda items to  be introduced to the series if  implemented in breadth the while - I  wouldn't change much to its  functionality except for the way you  control it I can definitely see the  beetle working great with the gyro amy  using slight tilts of the switch or pro  controller to change direction at the  same time having the option to use the  analog stick as an alternative would be  nice - not everyone enjoys having to  tilt their controller or switch at  awkward angles luckily Nintendo seems to  have learned from its past mistakes and  already gave this option in both breath  the wild and Mario Odyssey breath the  wild rewarded creativity by playing  around with the physics and trying out  all kinds of different things the beetle  would definitely supplement this for  some next-level strategies being able to  pick up small rocks explosive barrels or  other items and bombard enemy camps fly  straight into enemies like a kamikaze  pilot and if the chicest leg were to  make a return or at the very least  remote bombs dropping a bomb picking it  up with the beetle and turning it into a  b-17 bomber the sky is the limit  another honorable mention goes to Andrew  Chapman who suggested something similar  but rather than the actual beetle it  would be a boomerang that behaves  similarly  this one's from werewolf 9 1/4 instead  of just using a glorified vacuum cleaner  he presents the idea of pointing it onto  the ground and blasting a gust of air to  launch yourself upwards a bit like  Rivoli's gale but faster and with less  height as not to make it to Opie so  basically we are rocket jumping like in  quake but without blowing your legs to  pieces and hurting yourself with each  jump I never found the gust gr to be a  particularly interesting item especially  in Skyward Sword  but if used in this manner I can imagine  this being tons of fun to use especially  when combined with the  glider Paulie Griffin also came up with  a lot of ideas so I again had to choose  one a portable Guardian laser like the  one the blight cannons are carrying the  most likely way I would see this being  implemented is if Lynx hand is able to  transform into different types of  devices again like in the concept art  and I am all for it let's go full  Megaman let's give Samus a run for our  money and give link a freaking arm  cannon tech mean why not write an  alternative to this being one of Link's  hand morphing abilities would be if it  simply functions as a regular weapon  with limited durability similar to the  different elemental rods found in breath  the wild perhaps this could even be an  item that can be crafted by none other  than Robbie I mean he is the expert at  ancient weapon technology after all  maybe if given the right parts he could  extract the firing mechanism from a  guardian and turn it into a cannon  capable of being wielded by a human well  get on it old man the last one comes  from evil tada 9 a wolf transformation  to jump further track smell or to run  faster I'm a bit conflicted about this  one since when it comes to the main  gimmick of a game they never repeat it  twice in the exact same manner we did  have the option to put wolf link in  breath the wild through the use of  amiibos but this worked very differently  I personally don't think they would  allow link to transform into a wolf  himself as that has already been done  before Nintendo usually strives for  something new however there is an  alternative in creating a champion it  reads that wolf link was actually a  toned down version of an idea they had  in mind during the early stages of  development this creature would have  been able to receive commands navigate  fight alongside you follow you around  and even talk perhaps we could see a  more fleshed-out version of this  returning in the sequel where you can  give actual commands like in fallout 4  or even take control of your companion  temporarily and as you stated in your  idea track sense jump gaps or crawl  through small spaces that link cannot  reverse it switches for you etc and that  is a wrap  or this one all of these ideas at the  same time would probably be too much for  the zelda team to handle but we can hope  that at least some of these ideas make  it into the new game I want to have some  closing words before I end this video  first off a big thank you to everyone  who supported me so far I only started  uploading content a little over a month  ago and the warm welcome I've received  is more than I could have ever wished  for to all of you who subscribed  commented on my videos giving me  feedback and ideas or corrected mistakes  and oversights it's very much  appreciated I had a lot of fun making  this video and going through all of your  ideas we can do something similar for  the next milestone or maybe by that time  there's something else you would like me  to cover as for the near future since I  surpassed the 1k subscribers I will soon  be able to make community posts right  here on YouTube I think it takes about a  week for it to activate so from that  point on I will be able to give you guys  two direct updates on projects that I'm  working on I'm not exactly a social  media person but I am considering  setting up a Twitter account as well as  an alternative way to communicate with  you all so when I get around to it I  will let you know about it in terms of  upcoming projects I have a couple of  different things on the way since you  guys seem to really appreciate my take  on Zelda lore I will be doing those more  often however I will not stop doing game  analysis and mechanics either as a  matter of fact I have two different  videos about game mechanics planned both  of which will be collaborations for one  of them I will once again be modeling a  dungeon idea in blender so I hope you  look forward to that these videos will  drop around mid to late June at the  earliest as I'm of course dependent on  other people's schedules as for the  upcoming weeks I have two different  videos planned I want to do another lore  video and I also want to do a more  personal video about my experience with  breath the wild and why I think the game  is such an important milestone now for  my question to you guys and gals is  which video would you prefer to see for  next week lore or a more personal tale  be sure to let me know down in the  comments one quick final notice I've had  a couple of people requesting me to post  my edit of the breath the wild 2 trailer  as a separate video and the answer to  that is yes I'm going to do some little  touch-ups on the sound of the trailer  and maybe even pay a professional to mix  and master  so it can be the best it can possibly be  if and when my channel gets monetized I  will make sure that this video will not  have any ads on it  so you can always watch it without  interruption I will also provide a  download link to the original mp4 in  case anyone wants to use it for whatever  personal purpose if you want to stay up  to date on my latest uploads consider  subscribing hitting the Bell you know  how it goes thank you all for watching  and I will see you in the next video  this is Don signing off and have a good  one

